Originally reported on Google Code with ID 2733
What archive revision are you testing on? 0.8.9.16

If appropriate, enter the URL of a page where the problem can be seen:
code at: http://archiveofourown.org/skins/431

What is the expected output? What do you see instead?
Skin is designed to break block of texts into each category and add type headers and
does wonderfully for that. However, code inserts "Freeform: " label, which isn't used
elsewhere in user-facing portions of the Archive. (Insert obligatory wrangler grumble
here. ^^ ) ByLine should insert "Additional Tags: " in the affected locations.

Please use labels and text to provide additional information.
User submitted code, may require user approval to alter.

Corrected last four lines of code:

li.characters + li.freeforms:before {
  content: "Additional Tags: ";
  color: #111;
  font-weight: bold;
}

li.warnings + li.characters:before {
  content: "Characters: ";
  color: #111;
  font-weight: bold;
}

li.warnings + li.freeforms:before {
  content: "Additional Tags: ";
  color: #111;
  font-weight: bold;
}

li.relationships + li.freeforms:before {
  content: "Additional Tags: ";
  color: #111;
  font-weight: bold;
}

